# JavaScript Module Rules

All JavaScript modules in Fibr follow strict patterns. Reference [src/extension/popup.js](mdc:src/extension/popup.js) for main structure.

## Module Pattern (IIFE)

All modules MUST use IIFE pattern:

```javascript
(function() {
  const ModuleName = {
    method: function() {
      // implementation
    }
  };
  window.ModuleName = ModuleName;
})();
```

## Module Loading

Modules augment main class prototype in [src/extension/popup.js](mdc:src/extension/popup.js):

```javascript
window.TabTalkAPI && Object.assign(l.prototype, window.TabTalkAPI);
window.TabTalkTwitter && Object.assign(l.prototype, window.TabTalkTwitter);
```

## Key Modules

- [src/extension/modules/twitter.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/twitter.js) - Main generation engine (3,014 lines)
- [src/extension/modules/api.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/api.js) - API wrapper with retry logic
- [src/extension/modules/gallery.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/gallery.js) - Gallery system (50-item limit)
- [src/extension/modules/storage.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/storage.js) - Chrome Storage wrapper
- [src/extension/modules/validation.js](mdc:src/extension/modules/validation.js) - API key validation

## Code Patterns

### Defensive Programming
```javascript
if (this.pageContent && this.pageContent.length > 0) {
  // proceed
} else {
  // fallback with error handling
}
```

### Storage Operations
```javascript
// Use abstraction methods, not direct chrome.storage
await this.getStorageItem('geminiApiKey');
await this.setStorageItem('theme', 'dark');
```

### Error Handling
```javascript
try {
  // operation
} catch (error) {
  if (error.message && error.message.includes("Extension context invalidated")) {
    // handle gracefully
  }
  throw error;
}
```

## Service Worker Communication

All API calls go through [src/extension/background.js](mdc:src/extension/background.js):

```javascript
chrome.runtime.sendMessage({
  action: 'callGeminiAPI',
  payload: { contents: conversation },
  apiKey: this.apiKey
}, response => {
  if (response.success) {
    // handle success
  }
});
```

## Content Extraction

Content script [src/extension/content.js](mdc:src/extension/content.js) returns:

```javascript
return { success: boolean, content: string, error?: string };
```

## Character Counting

Unicode-aware counting:

```javascript
function countCharacters(text) {
  return [...text].length; // Grapheme-aware counting
}
```

## Prohibited Patterns

- No ES6 modules (import/export)
- No direct chrome.storage calls (use abstraction)
- No eval() or dynamic code execution
- No console.log in production code
- No debug code in committed files
